      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Felicia being taken down by the mining l.a.s.e.r. makes me think of a power defining argument that I am sure happens a lot online and in editorial of the comics-\nHow does \"Single Attack Negation\" work against a prolonged beam or continuous aura? In theory the mining l.a.s.e.r. does not fire a shot like a gun but generates a beam that only stops when you turn the Device off. Does \"Single Attack Negation\" protect for the first 6 second of the beam? the first Minute? until the \"one attack\" of the beam ends?\n\nand for those who liked my first comment it was not just the shanty but the performers I like",
